From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JalenLin <jalen.lin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:04:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/22] net: realtek: add the RTD1295 NAT engine's port 5 as a
 NIC

The second RJ45 of the BPI-W2: port 5 (RGMII0) of the SoC's hardware NAT
engine, an RTL8197F-style switch core, used as a plain network interface.
The driver, rtd1295-hwnat.c, is kept outside the kernel tree in kernel/src
and copied in by scripts/build-kernel.sh; these lines hook it in.

Source: https://github.com/JalenLin/BPI-W2-linux

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 .../bindings/net/realtek,rtd1295-hwnat.yaml   |  101 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Kconfig          |   16 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/Makefile         |    1 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/rtd1295-hwnat.c  | 1644 +++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 1762 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/realtek,rtd1295-hwnat.yaml
